  "description": "Fuji builds two Roubaix models.\nThey're dual-spec bikes, bikes with identical or near-identical equipment\nmade from two different materials. Roubaix Pro is the steel one, its main\nframe made from Reynolds legendary 853 Air-Hardened Tubes. Eight-five-three\ngrows stronger from the welding torch's heat. Other steel tubes weaken.\nA properly designed 853 bike will have all of steel's great qualities,\nsteel's ride and resilience and traditional appearance. It'll be slightly\nheavier than a bike made from X-Fusion aluminum, but as many veteran cyclists\nwill tell you, it'll be the joy to ride that steel bikes have been for\n100-plus years.\n\nRoubaix Pros have two chainrings. Roubaixs have three. If you live in\nflat country or you're a pretty strong climber, two is all you need. Roubaix\nPros have super-cool carbon fiber forks and cool Ritchey Pro wheels.\n\nYou'd buy a Roubaix Pro because you've decided maybe your local club's\ntraining rides aren't too fast for you after all. You might buy one to\nride your fastest-ever Hotter 'n' Hell Hundred. You may be planning a\nsupported ride across some state, Ohio maybe, and you want to ride the\n85 miles/day with the fast group.\nYou go, girl.",
